---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Redactor from '../components/Redactor.jsx';
---
<Base path="/redact-image/" title="Redact Images Online — Blackout, Pixelate & Blur | PlainMile"
  description="Manually hide parts of JPG, PNG and WebP images with solid blocks, real pixelation or blur. Preview every change and export locally, including batch ZIP.">
  <section class="page-head">
    <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Image tools</a> / Redact images</p>
    <h1>Manually redact images and screenshots</h1>
    <p class="lead">Draw a rectangle over text, faces, license plates or anything you want to hide. Choose solid color, pixelation or blur and preview the real effect before exporting.</p>
  </section>
  <Redactor client:load lang="en"/>
  <section class="reference">
    <h2>How to cover parts of an image</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Choose JPG, PNG or WebP files, drag and drop them, or paste a screenshot. You can work on up to 12 images.</li>
      <li>Choose a style: solid color (black, white or custom), pixelation or blur. Adjust intensity for pixelation and blur.</li>
      <li>Drag a rectangle directly over the area to cover. Each new rectangle uses the currently selected style. Remove mistaken rectangles or use Undo and Redo.</li>
      <li>Inspect the rendered preview, choose PNG, JPG or WebP, then download one image or a ZIP of your reviewed batch.</li>
    </ol>
    <h2>Blackout, pixelation or blur?</h2>
    <p>Use a solid opaque color for passwords, addresses, IDs, access keys, account details and any information that must be hidden. Solid redaction replaces the underlying pixels. Pixelation and blur are visual effects that can still reveal or leak information. Their real results, not translucent placeholders, are shown in the editor.</p>
    <h2>Is text detected automatically?</h2>
    <p>No. This editor is intentionally manual-only. Photographs, technical equipment and patterned backgrounds can lead to unreliable automated suggestions. You choose every region. Review the result carefully before sharing; no recognition tool can guarantee that every secret is covered.</p>
    <h2>Can I redact several images?</h2>
    <p>Yes. Every image keeps its own rectangles and Undo/Redo history. Batch ZIP export requires at least one manually drawn cover on each image, to prevent accidentally including an unredacted file. ZIP members are named generically instead of using potentially sensitive source filenames.</p>
    <h2>Privacy, sizes and formats</h2>
    <p>All image editing and ZIP generation happens inside your browser. Images are not uploaded. Re-encoded exports discard source EXIF metadata. Supports JPEG, PNG and WebP; up to 12 images and 100 MB total, 32 megapixels per image and 96 megapixels per batch. Read the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>
    <h2>Related tools</h2>
    <ul class="related-links">
      <li><a href="/resize-image/">Resize image</a></li>
      <li><a href="/compress-image-to-size/">Compress to KB</a></li>
      <li><a href="/bulk-image-resizer/">Bulk resize</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Base>
